<section class="engagement-stages material-notes section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">What takes shape</p><div class="process-grid"><article><span class="drawing-number">01 / Feasibility</span><h3>A grounded brief.</h3><p>Site observations, an outline of constraints, early layout options and an agreed list of priorities. A point to decide whether and how to proceed.</p></article><article><span class="drawing-number">02 / Design</span><h3>A coherent proposal.</h3><p>Plans and spatial studies bring scale, light and material choices together. Reviews allow the direction to develop with your feedback.</p></article><article><span class="drawing-number">03 / Coordination</span><h3>A resolved set of details.</h3><p>Drawings and specifications are developed with the appointed specialists. The agreed scope defines the information needed for the next stage.</p></article></div><p class="small">Illustrative service description. Deliverables, approvals, costs and programme would be confirmed in a written appointment.</p></div></section>
